      "text": "To determine how many minutes it will take to print 200 pages at a rate of 17 pages per minute, we can use the following steps:\n\n1. Identify the total number of pages to be printed, which is 200 pages.\n2. Identify the printing rate, which is 17 pages per minute.\n3. Use the formula for time, which is the total number of pages divided by the printing rate. This formula is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time (minutes)} = \\frac{\\text{Total pages}}{\\text{Printing rate}}\n   \\]\n4. Substitute the given values into the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time (minutes)} = \\frac{200 \\text{ pages}}{17 \\text{ pages per minute}}\n   \\]\n5. Perform the division to find the time:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time (minutes)} \\approx 11.7647\n   \\]\n6. Round the result to the nearest whole number:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time (minutes)} \\approx 12\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the time it will take to print 200 pages is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) minutes.",
