      "text": "To determine how many minutes it will take the printer to print 200 pages, we can use the given rate of the printer, which is 17 pages per minute. We need to find out how many minutes, \\( t \\), it will take for the printer to print 200 pages.\n\nThe relationship between the number of pages printed, the rate of printing, and the time taken can be expressed by the equation:\n\\[ \\text{Number of pages} = \\text{Rate} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the number of pages is 200, the rate is 17 pages per minute, and the time is \\( t \\) minutes. Plugging in these values, we get:\n\\[ 200 = 17 \\times t \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( t \\), we need to isolate \\( t \\) on one side of the equation. We do this by dividing both sides of the equation by 17:\n\\[ t = \\frac{200}{17} \\]\n\nNow, we perform the division:\n\\[ t \\approx 11.76 \\]\n\nSince the problem asks for the time to the nearest whole number, we round 11.76 to the nearest whole number, which is 12. Therefore, it will take approximately \\(\\boxed{12}\\) minutes to print 200 pages.",
